# Monolith MCP — Project Instructions

This project uses **Monolith** for Unreal Engine MCP integration. Tool and action totals are runtime-discovered; call `monolith_status()` for the current totals and `monolith_discover("namespace")` for live action schemas.

## Tools

- `monolith_discover(namespace?)` — List available actions (always call this first)
- `monolith_status()` — Health check, version, action count
- `monolith_reindex()` — Trigger full project re-index

## Namespace Query Tools

Use `{namespace}_query(action, params)` after discovering the namespace. Common in-tree namespaces include:

- `ai_query` — AI: Behavior Trees, State Trees, EQS, Smart Objects, Perception, Navigation
- `animation_query` — Animation assets, ABP, PoseSearch, montages
- `asset_query` — Asset registry inspection and asset metadata
- `audio_query` — Audio asset CRUD, Sound Cue/MetaSound graph building, AI perception binding
- `blueprint_query` — Blueprint CRUD, compile, nodes, spawn actors
- `chaos_fracture_query` — Chaos Fracture inspection and read-only utilities
- `chooser_query` — Chooser table inspection and validation
- `cloth_query` — Cloth asset inspection and validation
- `collection_query` — Collection inspection and maintenance
- `combograph_query` — ComboGraph combo systems
- `config_query` — Config/INI resolution
- `context_query` — Runtime/editor context inspection
- `dataflow_query` — Dataflow graph inspection
- `editor_query` — Build, logs, compile output, crash context, scene capture
- `gamefeatures_query` — Game Feature plugin inventory and GameFeatureData inspection
- `gas_query` — Gameplay Ability System: abilities, attributes, effects, ASC
- `hlod_query` — HLOD inspection and diagnostics
- `input_query` — Enhanced Input mapping inspection
- `interchange_query` — Interchange asset pipeline inspection
- `level_query` — Level actors, world state, and spatial inspection
- `level_instance_query` — Level Instance inspection
- `level_sequence_query` — Level Sequence inspection, bindings, director blueprints
- `localization_query` — Localization targets and text data
- `logicdriver_query` — Logic Driver Pro state machines
- `material_query` — Materials, instances, functions, HLSL, graph
- `mesh_query` — Mesh inspection, scene manipulation, spatial queries, blockout, GeometryScript
- `metahuman_query` — MetaHuman asset inspection
- `movie_render_query` — Movie Render Queue management
- `ndisplay_query` — nDisplay config inspection
- `niagara_query` — Niagara VFX, dynamic inputs, sim stages
- `paper2d_query` — Paper2D asset inspection
- `pcg_query` — PCG graph inspection
- `project_query` — Project-wide asset search
- `slate_query` — Live editor Slate window/widget inspection
- `source_control_query` — Source control status and workspace inspection
- `source_query` — Engine C++ source lookup, class hierarchy, callers/callees
- `ui_query` — Widget blueprints, templates, styling, accessibility
- `water_query` — Water/Landscape actor discovery
- `world_conditions_query` — World Conditions schema and asset inspection

## Workflow

1. Call `monolith_discover("namespace")` to see actions before guessing names
2. Use `project_query("search", {"query": "..."})` to find assets
3. Use `source_query("search_source", {"query": "..."})` to look up UE C++ APIs
4. Use domain tools to inspect/modify assets
5. After C++ changes: `editor_query("get_build_errors")` to check results

## Asset Paths

All paths use `/Game/Path/To/Asset` format (no `.uasset`):
- Project Content: `/Game/Path/To/Asset`
- Project Plugins: `/PluginName/PluginName/Path/To/Asset`
- Engine plugins: `/PluginName/Path/To/Asset`

## Rules

- Always discover before calling — action names change between versions
- Never guess `#include` paths or UE API signatures — use `source_query` to verify
- The project index is pre-built — use `project_query` for broad searches
- For material work: `create_material` → `build_material_graph` → `connect_expressions` → `recompile_material`
